<!doctype html>
<html class="js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    {%- comment -%}
      Minimal layout for the Black Friday 2026 landing page.

      The page renders its own header, footer and cart drawer, so this layout
      deliberately omits the theme's header-group, footer-group, cart drawer and
      component stylesheets — none of it is visible on this template, and
      loading it would only cost the campaign page weight it does not need.

      What stays is what a standalone page still has to have: Shopify's own
      content_for_header (apps, analytics, consent), the storefront page-view
      event so campaign traffic is still attributed, SEO/meta tags, and the
      cart routes the section's forms post to.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0908">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Campaign SEO and share card. Set here rather than left to the theme's
      meta-tags snippet, which falls back to the store name: the shop has no
      meta description, so a shared link would preview as just "Malbor Coatings
      USA". This layout serves only the campaign, so the copy belongs to it.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- assign lp_title = 'Black Friday at Malbor — Professional Line 25% off' -%}
    {%- assign lp_description = 'Black Friday 2026: 25% off every Professional Line 60ml ceramic coating, 35% off when you buy 5, and a free SiO2 Top Sealant with every bottle. November 27–30. Local pickup in Pompano Beach and Fort Lauderdale. While supplies last.' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The teaser section (sections/lp-blackfriday-teaser.liquid) runs before
      the offer is announced, so its share card must not mention it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if content_for_layout contains 'data-lp-teaser' -%}
      {%- assign lp_title = 'Black Friday is coming to Malbor — Nov 27' -%}
      {%- assign lp_description = 'The Malbor Professional Line goes on sale on Black Friday, November 27. Ceramic coatings for the boat, the car and the interior. Local pickup in Pompano Beach and Fort Lauderdale.' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Share card: a 1200x630 image made for the campaign (source in
      media/black-friday/share), so a link pasted in WhatsApp or Instagram
      shows Black Friday rather than a single product photo.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if content_for_layout contains 'data-lp-teaser' -%}
      {%- assign lp_image = 'lp-blackfriday-share-teaser.jpg' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign lp_image = 'lp-blackfriday-share-offer.jpg' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>{{ lp_title }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ lp_description | escape }}">

    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ lp_title | escape }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ lp_description | escape }}">
    {%- if lp_image != blank -%}
      <meta property="og:image" content="{{ lp_image }}">
      <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
      <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
      <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ lp_image }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ lp_title | escape }}">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ lp_description | escape }}">

    {{ content_for_header }}

    <script type="module">
      import * as StandardEvents from 'https://cdn.shopify.com/storefront/standard-events.js';

      window.StandardEvents = StandardEvents;

      document.addEventListener(
        'DOMContentLoaded',
        () => {
          const template = document.querySelector('main[data-template]')?.dataset.template || '';
          document.dispatchEvent(
            new StandardEvents.PageViewEvent({
              page: { template, title: document.title, url: window.location.href },
            })
          );
        },
        { once: true }
      );
    </script>

    {% style %}
      *,
      *::before,
      *::after {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      html {
        height: 100%;
      }

      body {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        min-height: 100%;
        margin: 0;
        /* Matches --lp-bg so no theme colour shows through above the fold. */
        background: #0b0908;
      }

      main {
        flex: 1;
      }
    {% endstyle %}
  </head>

  <body>
    <a class="lp-skip" href="#MainContent">Skip to content</a>

    <main id="MainContent" role="main" tabindex="-1" data-template="{{ template.name }}">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    <script>
      window.shopUrl = '{{ request.origin }}';
      window.routes = {
        cart_add_url: '{{ routes.cart_add_url }}',
        cart_change_url: '{{ routes.cart_change_url }}',
        cart_update_url: '{{ routes.cart_update_url }}',
        cart_url: '{{ routes.cart_url }}',
      };
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
